---
import DocsLayout from '@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Flow from '@/components/Flow.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---
<DocsLayout title="Methodology">
  <p class="docs-lead">
    How problems are built and verified. Full contract:
    <a href="https://github.com/shepardxia/ppl-gym/blob/main/data/SCHEMA.md"><code>data/SCHEMA.md</code></a>.
  </p>

  <Flow steps={[
    { t: 'sources', s: 'probmods · dippl · forest · posteriordb' },
    { t: 'problem statement', s: 'given / model / query<br/>+ typed answer spec' },
    { t: 'realizations', s: 'WebPPL · Pyro · Stan' },
    { t: 'two gates', s: 'solver re-derivation<br/>cross-language' },
    { t: 'verified dataset', s: '160 problems', tone: 'good' },
  ]} label="Statements are language-neutral prose that pin the answer and leave the program open. A ground truth ships after surviving both gates." />

  <h2>Measured tolerance</h2>
  <Flow steps={[
    { t: 'ground truth', s: 'k seeded runs' },
    { t: 'noise floor', s: 'max pairwise distance' },
    { t: 'tolerance', s: 'margin × floor' },
  ]} label="Each problem’s threshold comes from its own ground-truth noise: deterministic problems demand near-exact answers; stochastic ones get exactly the slack their sampling justifies." />

  <h2>Gate 1 — solver re-derivation</h2>
  <Flow steps={[
    { t: 'rendered statement', s: 'prose only — no code shown' },
    { t: 'independent solvers', s: '2 × LLM' },
    { t: 'judged vs ground truth', s: 'within measured tolerance' },
    { t: 'accept', tone: 'good' },
  ]} label="Solvers agreeing with each other but not the GT marks the GT suspect — investigated to a measured root cause before anything changes." />

  <h2>Gate 2 — cross-language consistency</h2>
  <Flow steps={[
    { t: 'WebPPL / gold-reference GT', s: 'k seeded runs' },
    { t: 'agree within margin × max(floors)', s: 'idiomatic library use, audited by judgment' },
    { t: 'Pyro / Stan GT', s: 'k seeded runs' },
  ]} label="Stronger than solver consensus, which shares the GT's blind spots — this gate caught a biased, already-accepted WebPPL ground truth. The posteriordb corpus crosschecks its Stan column against gold reference draws." />

  <h2>Provenance</h2>
  <p>
    Ground truth matching its textbook source is authoritative; statements are
    the rewritable layer. Source overrides require documented evidence of internal
    inconsistency. Retired problems are parked with reasons.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
